Yes. Mistral isn't a built-in provider, but its API is OpenAI-compatible, so add it as a custom provider in your `opencode.json`:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "mistral": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Mistral",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.mistral.ai/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "mistral-small-latest": { "name": "Mistral Small" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Then set your key via `/connect` (or `export MISTRAL_API_KEY=...` and add `"apiKey": "{env:MISTRAL_API_KEY}"`) and pick it with `/models`.

