The user wants to use the local Qwen model with opencode, so opencode can execute processes/tools. So they want to configure opencode to use the ollama model as its model provider. That way, I (opencode) would run on the local `uncut` model with full tool access.

This is a legitimate opencode configuration task. I should load the customize-opencode skill since this involves configuring opencode itself (provider/models in opencode.json).

Let me set up the config so opencode uses ollama's `uncut` model. The config:
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "ollama": {
      "models": {
        "uncut": { "name": "Uncut Qwen3-8B" }
      }
    }
  },
  "model": "ollama/uncut"
}
```

But wait — does the ollama provider config in opencode require npm package? The docs show ollama as a built-in provider (it's in the directory listing). Actually opencode supports ollama natively I believe. In the docs example they used `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` with baseURL localhost:11434/v1. But there may be a native ollama provider. Let me check opencode's model provider list. The safest is to use the openai-compatible approach with baseURL http://localhost:11434/v1 and model "uncut".

Note: ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint at /v1 — model id "uncut". opencode can use it via @ai-sdk/openai-compatible.

But there's a concern: an 8B abliterated model running local — tool calling quality may be limited. Qwen3-8B has decent tool calling, but 8B models in opencode agent mode can be hit-or-miss. I should warn briefly but set it up.

The user should use the customize-opencode skill since we're editing opencode config. Let me load it.

Then check current opencode config location: ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json or in project. Working dir is /home/dpboom. Let me check existing config.

Let me load the skill first.

No config exists. I'll create a global config at ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json that:
1. Adds ollama provider with the uncut model
2. Sets the default model to ollama/uncut

The ollama provider in opencode: I'll verify whether it's built-in. Let me check the schema quickly to see if "ollama" is a known provider id, or just use the openai-compatible approach which is documented. The docs example for Ollama in the providers page used:

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "ollama": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Ollama (local)",
      "options": { "baseURL": "http://localhost:11434/v1" },
      "models": { "uncut": { "name": "Uncut Qwen3" } }
    }
  }
}
```

Then `"model": "ollama/uncut"`.

Let me also add the base model maybe. And keep small_model default? Not needed.

Also, the apiKey: ollama local doesn't need one, but opencode may require an apiKey field for custom providers. Some setups use a dummy key like "ollama". Let me include `"apiKey": "ollama"` in options to be safe — the docs' Atomic Chat example didn't include it though. I'll follow the docs example exactly (no apiKey). If opencode errors, user can add.

